## Intuition
We need to find the minimum day on which it is possible to make at least m bouquets. Each bouquet requires exactly k adjacent bloomed flowers.

One important observation is that if we can make m bouquets on a certain day, then we can also make them on all later days because more flowers will have bloomed. This gives us a monotonic property, which suggests using Binary Search on the answer.

## Approach
First, check if it is even possible to make the required bouquets. If m * k > n, return -1.

Use Binary Search on the number of days. For a given day, traverse the array and count consecutive flowers that have bloomed **(nums[i] <= day)**.

Whenever the count reaches k, we can form one bouquet and reset the count. At the end, if the number of bouquets formed is at least m, then that day is a valid answer.

If a day is valid, try to find a smaller valid day by searching on the left half. Otherwise, search on the right half.

The first valid day found will be the minimum number of days required.

